# ============================================================================
# F-STOP repo .gitignore
#
# Policy: this repository ships the F-STOP port plus the engine binaries that
# upstream (sears2424/Enhanced-Source) ships - game/bin, game/core, game/platform
# and the launchers. Retail game content and the Portal 2 2009 depot are IGNORED
# (not deleted) so local dev keeps working but they can never enter a commit; that
# content comes from the player's own installed copy.
# The ignore list mirrors upstream where it does not conflict with the above - see
# the upstream-parity block below.
# ============================================================================

# --- retail trees (provided by the player's own install) ---
/game/hl2_template/
/game/template/
/game/template_additional_content/
/game/sdk_content/
/game/deferred/
/game/vectronic/
/game/hl2.exe
/game/hl2.wrap.exe

# --- engine/SDK build outputs and IDE cruft (regenerated from src/) ---
/game/portal_template/bin/
/src/.vs/
**/.vs/
*.sln.bak
/src/UpgradeLog.htm
/src/devtools/bin/*.dll

# --- compiler/build intermediates (never source) ---
# shaderlib.lib is a build output, rewritten by every ShaderLib build. It used to be
# tracked (upstream ships prebuilt libs) but that leaves the tree permanently dirty.
/src/lib/public/shaderlib.lib
*.obj
*.pdb
*.tlog
*.idb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.sbr
*.bsc
/src/game/server/Debug_portal_template/
/src/game/client/Debug_portal_template/
/src/game/client/Debug_mod_hl2/
/src/materialsystem/shaderlib/Debug/
/src/materialsystem/stdshaders/Debug_dx9_portal/
/src/materialsystem/deferredshaders/Release_dx9/

# --- upstream parity: everything Enhanced Source's .gitignore skips ---
# Mirrors sears2424/Enhanced-Source/.gitignore so this repo ships exactly what
# upstream ships. The VS *project* files are VPC-generated (the .vpc sources ship, and
# vpc.exe is in src/devtools). The one *solution* is not reproducible though: VPC's -mksln
# needs the VS2013 project-file registration (VisualStudio.vcxproj.12.0), which a machine
# with only a newer Visual Studio does not have - it writes every .vcxproj and then
# abandons the solution. So src/Game_Portal_Template-2019.sln ships with the repo
# (re-included below) and the build works on any machine.
*.suo
*.user
*.sln.docstates
*.scc
*.lastbuildstate
*.pch
*.sdf
*.opensdf
ipch/
*.VC
*.VC.VC.opendb
*.VC.db
vc100.pdb
*.vpc_crc
*.vpc.sentinel
*.sln
!/src/Game_Portal_Template-2019.sln
*.vcxproj
*.vcxproj.filters
*.log
hammer.vdf
GameConfig.txt
/game/hl2/
/game/portal/
/src/game/client/Debug*/
/src/game/client/Release*/
/src/game/server/Debug*/
/src/game/server/Release*/

# --- runtime junk ---
/game/portal_template/console*.log
/game/portal_template/*.tmp
/game/portal_template/*.dt
/game/portal_template/SAVE/
/game/portal_template/stats.txt
/game/portal_template/tilegen_log.txt
/game/portal_template/modelsounds.cache
# engine runtime state - the game rewrites this on launch
/game/portal_template/cfg/config.cfg
/game/portal_template/voice_ban.dt
/game/portal_template/maps/soundcache/
/game/portal_template/screenshots/
/game/portal_template/cfg/*.bak

# --- Source engine crash dumps (minidumps written on a hard crash) ---
*.mdmp
*.dmp


# NOTE: CS:GO/L4D2-sourced assets (particles/rain_fx.pcf, some particle .vtf) are
# intentionally KEPT in the mod - those games ship VPK v2, which this engine
# cannot mount ("Unknown version 2 for vpk"), so the mod must carry them itself.
/game/retail/

